 "result": "Both live in `src/tessel/cli.py`. This repo is a renamed Flask, so the names differ from Flask's.\n\n- **Decorator: `needs_app_scope`** (`src/tessel/cli.py:380`). This is Flask's `with_appcontext`. If no app is active yet, it loads the app through `LaunchInfo` and pushes `app.app_context()` before running your command.\n- **Loader class: `LaunchInfo`** (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`). This is Flask's `ScriptInfo`. Its `load_app()` method (`src/tessel/cli.py:333`) finds the app in this order: `create_app`, then `--app` / `TESSEL_APP`, then `wsgi.py` / `app.py`. It caches the result. `pass_script_info` (`src/tessel/cli.py:375`) passes it into a command.\n\nYou may not need the decorator. Commands registered on `app.cli` or `bundle.cli`, or on any `AppGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`), are wrapped in `needs_app_scope` automatically. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to turn that off. Use the decorator directly only on plain `click` commands.",
